  "id": "Compound::DB01327 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Cefazolin, a member of the cephalosporin class, is linked to Slc22a11 through a shared biological pathway involving antibiotics that bind to this transporter. The evidence suggests that Cefazolin, along with other cephalosporins like cefoperazone and cefotaxime, binds to Slc22a11, which is a member of the Slc22 family of transporters. This relationship is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) structure, where Cefazolin and its related antibiotics are grouped under the broader category of cephalosporins, which in turn bind to Slc22a11. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a strong, reliable connection between Cefazolin and Slc22a11, likely due to the shared mechanism of action and the presence of a common biological target. The integration of these paths highlights a recurring mechanism of antibiotic binding to transporters, suggesting that Slc22a11 may play a critical role in the pharmacological action of cephalosporins.",
